From: guydidosh <guydidosh@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 16:46:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat: a nodepool's annotations reach the NodePool

An entry's `annotations:` map is now rendered onto its NodePool, values as
strings, next to the chart's own argocd.argoproj.io/sync-wave (which an entry
may not set: the render fails, naming it). Labels are unchanged: still only
allowDeletion, maxReplicas and minReplicas.

The workflows' update-nodepool reads redbull.io/scale-down-policy
(fewest-pods, least-requested, least-utilized) off the NodePool to choose which
servers leave a scale-down; this is how it is written in the values repo.

With no annotations in an entry the render is unchanged: the golden parity
tests pass, and the sandbox's ocp4-upgrade-demo renders byte for byte as before.
